WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.000
While many fans couldn't really make sense
of Jared Leto's Joker in Suicide Squad, there's

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.370
no arguing against the fact that the movie's
Clown Prince of Crime had a really unique

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.370
look.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.360
But now, writer-director David Ayer has confessed
that he made a mistake with the character's

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.360
design.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.020
Whether you love it or you hate it, Jared
Leto's Joker design makes an impression.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.710
From his pale white skin and bright green
hair to his eye-catching tattoos and silver

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.300
teeth, he has a look that screams "gangster
meets prankster".

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.220
But was this stylized design really the right
approach?

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.700
Over two years after Suicide Squad's theatrical
run, Ayer has confessed that he now considers

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.510
one particular piece of Leto's Joker design
to be a total mistake.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.070
The admission came about thanks to a fan on
Twitter, who asked Ayer about the Joker's

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.830
eye-catching forehead tattoo the one that
simply reads: "Damaged".

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:50.210
When asked what inspired that particular bit
of ink, Ayer admitted that it was his idea

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.570
and he regrets it.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.480
The director responded to the query with a
mea culpa, writing,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.640
"Yes I have to fall on that sword.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.410
It was one step too far."

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.690
Even after owning up to what he now feels
was a bad move, Ayer affirmed that he still

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.470
generally likes the tattoo, at least in concept.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.210
He also gave some insight into his thought
process as to why the Joker would have such

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.440
a statement scribbled across his cranium.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.950
In a follow-up post, Ayer wrote,

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:18.650
"In my mind it was meant for Batman after
he smashed Joker['s] teeth for killing Jason

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.650
Todd.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.220
Some people found it alienating.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.090
Originality and faithfulness to the canon
are often at odds.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:27.390
Batman and Joker are my two favorite characters
ever."

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:31.890
Ayer offered a similar explanation for the
Joker's "damaged" tattoo around the time Suicide

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.440
Squad launched in theaters, saying that Joker
would have gotten the tattoo while locked

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.700
up in Arkham Asylum after being scooped up
by the Dark Knight.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.890
As he told Empire in August 2016,

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.990
"It's in the asylum where Joker would have
done the 'damaged' tattoo as a message to

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.110
Batman saying, 'You've damaged me.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:50.229
I was so beautiful before and now you've destroyed
my face.'

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:52.130
That's where the grill comes from."

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.760
As it happens, Ayer has quite a few regrets
about the decisions he made with Suicide Squad,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.530
many of which come down to choices made about
the Joker.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:03.560
Not only does Ayer now wish he didn't ink
up the Joker's forehead, he also regrets not

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.909
making the character the main bad guy of the
movie's story.

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:10.840
Despite being heavily featured in the movie's
promotional materials, Jared Leto's Joker

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.370
only has about ten total minutes of screen
time in the theatrical cut of Suicide Squad

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.840
far less than what was originally shot for
the supervillain picture.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.650
Even people who enjoyed the movie have said
that it could have been improved by an increased

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:26.980
focus on the evil jester, and some have approached
Ayer on Twitter with their thoughts.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.710
In response to one fan who wrote him a year
after the movie's release, Ayer said,

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.710
"Believe me.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.140
I agonize over this.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.140
Yes.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.940
Joker should have been [the] main bad guy."

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:36.940
"Yeah."

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.790
Ayer has been expressing some disappointment
in the final cut of Suicide Squad since shortly

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.600
after the film opened in theaters.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:48.450
In January 2017, the director penned a lengthy
post detailing what he wished he'd done differently,

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.380
then shared a screenshot of the note on his
Twitter page.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:55.540
In the post, he wished for a time machine
to undo the errors that he feels he made,

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.990
along with a determination to do better next
time.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.660
As for what he'd do differently, he said,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.400
"I'd make Joker the main villain and engineer
a more grounded story.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.680
I have to take the good and bad and learn
from it […] I have to give the characters

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.160
the stories and plots they deserve next time.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.160
Real talk."

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.320
As we know now, he'd also do away with that
distracting tattoo.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.330
Ayer's self-criticism is refreshing, but he
doesn't have to be so tormented.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.349
As divisive as Suicide Squad turned out to
be upon release, the movie still performed

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:25.210
well enough for Warner Bros. and DC to turn
a massive profit off of it.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.550
And despite the critical drubbing, plenty
of fans still truly enjoyed the film, Joker

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.550
and all.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:34.099
It can even be argued that Ayer crafted the
most unforgettable version of the Joker that

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:38.570
has yet to grace the screen, making a major
impact on pop culture despite the character's

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:39.630
slight screen time.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:43.660
Like the rest of Suicide Squad, Ayer's Joker
isn't necessarily a disaster.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.120
It's just a little damaged.

